  "_devices_doc": "For each partner device type (機器種別), the supported source/destination devices and their valid number ranges. 'base' is 10 (decimal) or 16 (hex). 'kind' is 'bit' or 'word'. 'min'/'max' are the inclusive integer bounds (in base 10 internally; UI shows them in 'base'). 'pattern_only' restricts the device to a specific 通信パターン on the partner side: 'Read' means only allowed when 通信パターン=Read (because the device sits on the partner side as the source — i.e., timer/counter contacts which can only be read); 'Write' means only allowed when 通信パターン=Write (when partner is destination — which our manual says is NOT allowed for these). For the 自局 (own iQ-R) side, a separate own-station ruleset is used.",

